# Dynamic Dialect Inference & Hallucination Fix

You made an excellent architectural point: the pipeline should be zero-shot and agnostic. It should autonomously figure out if the movie is Ancient China, Cyberpunk Tokyo, or a 1920s Noir film without you having to configure settings.

## What caused the Hallucination and the Dialect mixup?

1. **Amnesia (The Dialect Issue)**: At the moment, the pipeline suffers from total amnesia. It translates one isolated 2-second snippet at a time (e.g. "Ni zhuo she me?"). Because the LLM cannot physically see the previous sentence or the plot of the movie, it defaults to modern, generic American English ("Yo, what's up?"). 
2. **The Output Loop (The Hallucination)**: In Segment 18, the LLM broke down and started looping its own prompt (`<|assistant|> `). This happened because the specific AI model we downloaded (Llama 3 base) uses different background control tokens than what I injected into the prompt. The model got confused by the structure and started babbling instead of executing.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [translate.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/stages/translate.py)

1. **The Dynamic Context Buffer**: We will not hardcode "Ancient China". Instead, I will modify the loop in `_do_translate` to accumulate the last 5 translated sentences. We will pass this "rolling memory" into the prompt. 
    - *Result*: As the LLM translates the movie, it will naturally read the previous lines, organically infer the tone/dialect from the scene, and match it.
2. **Harden the Prompt Structure**: I will strip out the confusing `<|system|>` pseudo-tags and use a highly strict, bullet-proof text block. I will also lock down the Stop Tokens to physically force the LLM to halt after it emits the dialogue.

## User Review Required
> [!CAUTION]
> Because it is currently using the wrong dialect, **we still need to wipe the polluted translations and restart the AI translation stage from Segment 0.** 
> 
> The TTS stage is currently chewing through Segment 250+ using the bad translations. If you approve this plan, I will wipe the slate clean, apply the Dynamic Context Buffer, and let the translation run again. (You won't lose the Stem Splits or the Whisper Transcriptions).
